sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Signer as Signer (Browser Webcam)
    participant Client as Frontend (useRecognitionStream.ts)
    participant Canvas as HTML5 Landmark HUD
    participant WS as WebSocket (FastAPI / Uvicorn)
    participant CV as OpenCV Frame Decoder
    participant MP as MediaPipe Holistic
    participant PyTorch as PyTorch Neural Engines
    participant Audio as Browser Speech Synthesis

    Note over Signer,WS: Step 1: Protocol Upgrade Handshake
    Client->>WS: GET /api/v1/ws/recognize HTTP/1.1 (Upgrade: websocket)
    WS-->>Client: HTTP 101 Switching Protocols

    Note over Client,WS: Step 2: Continuous 30 FPS Stream Loop
    loop Every 33 Milliseconds
        Signer->>Client: Webcam Video Frame (640x480)
        Client->>WS: Raw Binary ArrayBuffer (JPEG Blob Quality 0.70)
        WS->>CV: cv2.imdecode(np.frombuffer(...))
        CV->>MP: Extract 21 Hand Keypoints (x, y, z)
        MP->>PyTorch: Centered & Scale-Normalized Tensor [1, 126]
        PyTorch-->>WS: Top Prediction ('A', Confidence: 0.94)
        WS-->>Client: JSON RecognitionPayload
        Client->>Canvas: Batched Draw 21 Bones & Joint Dots (0.4ms)
        Client->>Client: Render Luminous Center Prediction Badge
    end

    Note over Client,Audio: Step 3: Sentence Commit & Audio Synthesis
    Client->>Audio: window.speechSynthesis.speak("HELLO")
    Audio-->>Signer: Audio Playback from Speakers

